hon`), and a second `PreToolUse(Bash)` guardrail, installed in every run mode with no switch, denies a raw module-wide `go test`, `go build` or `go vet`, a raw `go test` over the `tmux` or `llm` tier, and any command naming the gate-slot or strand-name environment variable, steering the session to `lym gate test`, and to a package-scoped compile check the hub's `refuse_raw` does not refuse, and a third `PreToolUse(Bash)` guardrail, installed in every run mode with no switch, denies an `rm` on a computed path (a command substitution or a variable expansion in the command) so no permission dialog stalls the run, and a fourth `PreToolUse(Bash)` guardrail, installed in every run mode with no switch, denies `sed -i`, `perl -i`, and a redirect, heredoc or `tee` into a source file, steering the session to read a file with Read and change it with Edit or Write; the python deny's steer carries the same edit rule. The engine announces each deny it installs to the session's system prompt, and every Claude session it launches with a run directory also gets the creel trust sentence, through one `append-system-prompt.txt` file named by `--append-system-prompt-file` on launch and resume, so a session knows the tool is unavailable before it tries one and follows `[creel]` mail from its hooks. The engine sets the prompt-cache TTL per role on launch and resume from `claude.yaml`'s `prompt_cache_ttl` and `prompt_cache_ttl_roles` (template: 5 minutes for `driver`, 1 hour for `webster` and `orch`, 5 minutes for every other role). `claude.yaml`'s `keep_warm_cap` (template 250s) and `keep_warm_cap_roles` set the per-role keep-warm cap beside them. The provider is swappable behind an **engine** seam; the engine is picked from the registry by `shuttle.yaml`'s `engine:` key, Claude being the one registered engine. Per-run `Model`/`Effort` knobs (`lym shuttle run --model`/`--effort`; effort values `low|medium|high|xhigh|max`, empty = provider default) are engine-validated, not policed by `Spec.validate`. `Spec.Version` is a programmatic engine-validated version pin (claudeengine composes the pinned model id; no CLI flag — consumers drive it via the model-spec notation's `v=` param). Starting a run returns only once its provider is past its startup gates, and a provider that never comes up is torn down (run dir and last pane capture kept) and reported as an error from `Start`, or as `died`/`timeout` from `Run`. ✅ Implemented. See the `internal/shuttleengine` package documentation.
